## B3. IPC spec (concrete, buildable)

### Control plane
**Frame format** (identical in all 5 languages — this is your first contract test):

```
magic:    u32 = 0x46504131 ("FPA1")
version:  u16
flags:    u16   (bit0=compressed_zstd, bit1=is_error, bit2=more_fragments)
length:   u32   (payload bytes, max 16 MiB)
req_id:   u64
payload:  protobuf Envelope
```

```protobuf
message Envelope {
  string method = 1;          // "etl.import.parquet", "flow.cycle.submit"
  uint64 corr_id = 2;
  uint64 deadline_ms = 3;
  string idempotency_key = 4;
  string trace_id = 5;
  string workspace_id = 6;
  string actor_id = 7;
  oneof body {
    bytes request = 8;         // method-specific message
    StreamChunk chunk = 9;
    Error error = 10;
    Cancel cancel = 11;
  }
  repeated ShmRef attachments = 12;   // bulk data, NOT inline
}
message ShmRef {
  string section_name = 1;    // "Local\\fpa-{session}-{ring}-{slot}"
  uint64 offset = 2;
  uint64 length = 3;
  uint64 sequence = 4;
  string arrow_schema_id = 5;
  uint32 row_count = 6;
  uint64 checksum_xxh3 = 7;
}
message Error { uint32 code=1; string message=2; string detail_json=3; bool retryable=4; }
```

### Transport matrix (choose per language, unify at handshake)

| Link | Transport | Auth | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rust ↔ Go | **Named pipe** (`winio` / `tokio::net::windows::named_pipe`) | `GetNamedPipeClientProcessId` + SID check + ACL | Both have first-class support; strongest peer identity |
| Rust ↔ Java | **Loopback TCP** (default) or named pipe via `RandomAccessFile` | Bearer token + PID via `GetExtendedTcpTable` | Netty/grpc can't do Windows pipes; don't fight it |
| Rust ↔ Elixir | **Loopback TCP** (`:gen_tcp`, `packet: 4`) | Bearer token + PID | BEAM has no pipe transport; `:gen_tcp` is rock solid |
| Rust ↔ UI | Tauri commands + local WebSocket | Tauri capability ACL | Native |
| Rust ↔ Excel XLL | Named pipe | SID + session token | Excel runs as same user |

**Loopback hardening (mandatory):** bind `127.0.0.1` only, `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE`, ephemeral port written to an ACL'd file readable only by the installing user, 32-byte random bearer token in the handshake, verify connecting PID's exe path is inside the install dir, explicit Windows Firewall inbound block rule for the exe. **Never** bind `0.0.0.0` unless LAN mode is explicitly enabled by the user.

### Data plane — three tiers by size

| Payload | Mechanism | Copies |
|---|---|---|
| < 64 KiB | Inline protobuf `bytes` | 1 |
| 64 KiB – 8 MiB | Arrow IPC stream over the socket | 1–2 |
| > 8 MiB | **Shared-memory Arrow IPC file** (mmap) | 0 |
| > 1 GiB / ETL staging | **Parquet file handoff** on disk + path in `ShmRef` | 0 (mmap) |
| Ad-hoc SQL from any process | **Arrow Flight SQL** served by Rust | 1 |

**Shared-memory ring design:**
```
Section "Local\fpa-{session}-ring-{n}"  (CreateFileMappingW, PAGE_READWRITE)
Header (4096 B, cache-line aligned):
  magic, version, slot_count, slot_size
  write_seq (AtomicU64), read_seq per consumer
  producer_pid, consumer_pids[], last_heartbeat[]
Slots: [ status(u32) | len(u64) | schema_id | Arrow IPC file bytes (8-byte aligned) ]
Sync: named mutex for slot claim + named event for "data ready"
GC:   consumer refcount in header; slot reusable when all consumers advanced
Crash: supervisor reclaims rings whose consumer PIDs are dead; zero stale handles
```

**Critical rules:**
- Arrow **IPC format**, not the C Data Interface (which is in-process FFI only — a common confusion).
- Alignment: 8-byte minimum, 64-byte preferred for SIMD. Verify per-language allocator behavior.
- **Decimal128(38, 6)** for money across all languages. Never float for currency.
- Cross-language conformance suite: golden `.arrows` files with known values (decimals, nulls, dicts, timestamps with tz, nested lists) that **every** language must read byte-identically. CI gate.
- Elixir is **control-plane only** — no mature Arrow implementation. (Explorer wraps Polars via Rust NIFs if you ever need it.)

