## C5. Excel integration (be realistic, be excellent)

**Three surfaces, correct order:**

1. **XLL add-in (Rust) — PRIMARY, P0.** Native Excel C API (`XLOPER12`), 64-bit + 32-bit builds. Works fully offline, no COM registration, no HTTPS, no .NET. Provides:
   - `=FPA.GET(module, lineitem, time, version, entity, …)` — array-returning, batched, cached
   - `=FPA.SET(...)` / `FPA.PUSH(range, mapping)` — write-back with transaction + validation
   - `=FPA.DIMS()`, `=FPA.MEMBERS()`, `=FPA.LINEAGE()`
   - Ribbon-lite via Add-ins tab; async UDFs for long queries
   - **Sign the XLL** and install to a Trusted Location (modern Excel blocks unsigned/MOTW XLLs)
2. **Office-JS task pane (TypeScript) — P1.** Rich UI: dimension picker, scenario switcher, variance explorer, lineage viewer. Runs in WebView2 inside Excel. Offline requires a local HTTPS origin with a trusted cert — ship a per-user generated cert or use the XLL to broker data and keep the pane purely presentational.
3. **Workbook import/export (Java) — P0.**

**Honest fidelity tiers (publish this table in your docs):**

| Tier | Guarantee |
|---|---|
| **Tier A — Lossless round-trip** | Values, number formats, fonts/fills/borders, column widths, merged cells, defined names, conditional formats, data validation, standard formulas, sheet structure. **All unknown XML parts preserved byte-for-byte** (charts, pivot caches, VBA project, Power Query, slicers, comments). |
| **Tier B — Read + evaluate** | ~250 most-used Excel functions. Documented list. Unsupported → `#FPA_UNSUPPORTED!` with a report, never a wrong number. |
| **Tier C — Preserve, don't touch** | VBA (never executed), pivot caches (not recalculated), charts (preserved; data refresh via documented ranges), Power Query, dynamic arrays/LAMBDA (flagged). |
| **Tier D — Explicitly unsupported** | Executing macros, XLSB write, Excel 2003 `.xls` write, guaranteed pivot recalc. |

**Implementation:** Apache POI `OPCPackage` + **direct XML surgery** on `xl/worksheets/*.xml` — patch only `<c>` value/formula nodes you own; leave everything else untouched. This is the *only* way to get real-world round-trip fidelity. Golden-file tests hash every preserved part.

**Excel model importer (P1, high value):** parse a workbook → infer dimensions from headers/ranges → propose a blueprint → user confirms mapping → generate modules + formulas. This is your migration wedge from spreadsheet hell.

**Also expose the model as SQL (P1, killer feature):** Rust serves **Arrow Flight SQL + an ODBC driver** over the DuckDB projection. Now Excel Power Query, Power BI Desktop, Tableau, and Access can query your FP&A model **offline**. Instant ecosystem, near-zero UI work.

