This is the part that determines success. **"Fully vibe coded" fails at this scale unless you install a rigorous engineering system around the agents.** The system below is the actual product you build first.

## E1. The oracle strategy (highest-leverage decision in the whole plan)

**Build a slow, obviously-correct reference implementation, then differential-test the fast one against it.**

```
crates/engine-ref/    # ~1500 LOC. Naive. HashMap<(Dim,Member), Decimal>.
                      # No SIMD, no blocks, no caching, no parallelism.
                      # Interprets the DSL directly from the AST.
                      # Written FIRST, from the spec, by a separate AI session.
crates/hyperblock/    # The fast engine. Must match engine-ref bit-for-bit.
```

Property test loop (`proptest`): generate random valid models + random edits → run both → assert identical results **and** identical error codes. Run 100K cases nightly. This single mechanism catches ~80% of the bugs AI will introduce in your engine, and it's the reason you can safely let agents optimize aggressively.

**Additional oracles:**
| Oracle | Checks |
|---|---|
| **DuckDB SQL** | Every aggregation, rollup, and slice query has a SQL equivalent. Differential-test them. |
| **LibreOffice headless** (`soffice --headless --convert-to`) | Offline Excel formula parity for the supported function set |
| **Excel COM on the dev box** | Ground-truth parity for the top 100 functions + round-trip fidelity |
| **Golden `.xlsx` files** | Hash every preserved XML part before/after round-trip |
| **Golden Arrow IPC files** | Cross-language byte-exact conformance |
| **Deterministic simulation testing** | Sync/merge/supervisor under seeded interleavings + injected crashes (FoundationDB style) |

## E2. The Finance Invariant Suite (blocking, always-on)

Every commit, every merge, every import, every scenario restore runs these. Encode as data so agents can extend them.

```
I01  Balance sheet: Assets == Liabilities + Equity (per entity, period, version, currency)
I02  Cash flow: closing cash == BS cash
I03  Indirect CF == Direct CF (same model)
I04  Every hierarchy rollup == sum of leaves × weights (all hierarchies, all as-of dates)
I05  Allocation: sum(targets) == source EXACTLY (zero penny drift)
I06  IC eliminations net to zero within tolerance; suspense accounted
I07  FX: translate→back-translate round-trip within tolerance; CTA reconciles
I08  Version copy is byte-identical to source at copy time
I09  TB import ties to cube actuals to the cent; unmapped rows quarantined, never dropped
I10  Deferred revenue: opening + billings − revenue == closing
I11  ARR: opening + new + expansion − contraction − churn == closing
I12  Fixed assets: opening NBV + additions − disposals − depreciation == closing NBV
I13  Debt: opening + drawdowns − repayments == closing; interest ties to rate × balance
I14  Headcount: opening + hires − exits ± transfers == closing; payroll ties to roster
I15  Inventory: opening + purchases − COGS ± adjustments == closing
I16  PoC revenue: cumulative revenue ≤ contract value; over/under billing ties to WIP
I17  No cell contains NaN/Inf; money never uses f64
I18  Determinism: same inputs, {1,2,4,8,16} threads → bit-identical outputs
I19  Audit chain verifies end-to-end; no gaps; checkpoints valid
I20  RBAC: no unauthorized value reachable via any API, aggregate, or export
I21  Undo/redo: N ops then N undos → identical model hash
I22  Crash recovery: kill -9 at any of 50 injection points → WAL replay → identical state
I23  DuckDB rebuild from Parquet+CAS → identical query results
I24  Merge never produces a state violating I01–I16
I25  Round-trip xlsx: all preserved parts byte-identical
