## THE ONE-PARAGRAPH SUMMARY

Keep your five-language ambition, but give each language a **replaceable, contract-bounded job** and move numerics out of Elixir into Rust. Make **Rust the sole owner of state** — one DuckDB writer, one durable SQLite truth, one Arrow hub. Replace pointers-over-pipes with **named shared-memory sections + Arrow IPC**, replace gRPC-over-pipes with **framed Protobuf over per-language-native transports**, replace CRDTs with **semantic 3-way merge with human conflict resolution**, replace "100% Excel fidelity" with **surgical OpenXML patching plus published fidelity tiers**, and replace GraalVM with **jlink + AOT cache**. Then — before writing a single feature — build the three things that make AI-driven development survive contact with a financial engine: **a naive reference oracle, 28 executable finance invariants, and a CI gauntlet that agents cannot argue with.** Ship a narrow, numerically flawless, genuinely offline V1 in the beachhead vertical at month 12–15, and add industry breadth as declarative blueprint packs forever after. The engine's correctness is the product; everything else is packaging.